# Used automatically by `npm run build`. Vite prefers mode-specific env files
# over .env, so production builds cannot accidentally ship the dev URL —
# which is exactly what happened once: a build made with .env pointing at
# localhost:8787 was deployed, and every visitor's browser tried to call
# their own machine.
#
# Not a secret: this is a public endpoint, and committing it is what makes a
# deploy reproducible from a clean checkout.
VITE_API_ENDPOINT="https://travel-agent-backend.prashannapaudel2.workers.dev"
